---
import LegalPage from '../../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site.js';
---

<LegalPage
  title="Company Information"
  description="Legal identity, registered address, website operator, contact details and certification information for Shandong Sishui Haiyun Grain Machine Co., Ltd."
  lede="This page identifies the company behind flourmillingpro.com and the information buyers usually request during supplier qualification."
>
  <h2>1. Legal identity</h2>
  <table>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th>Legal name</th><td>{site.legalName}</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Brand</th><td>Haiyun Milling / HAIYUN</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Legal form</th><td>Limited liability company registered in the People's Republic of China</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Established</th><td>2010; manufacturing heritage from the former Shandong Flour Machinery Factory (production from 1963)</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Registered / operating address</th><td>{site.address.full}</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Business</th><td>Design, manufacture, supply and commissioning of wheat flour milling plants and grain-processing equipment</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>2. Website operator and responsibility for content</h2>
  <p>
    This website is operated by {site.legalName}. The company is responsible for the editorial and
    commercial content published on flourmillingpro.com. The website is a business-to-business
    information and enquiry channel; it is not a marketplace and does not accept payment-card
    transactions.
  </p>
  <p>
    Editorial responsibility: {site.name} technical content team. Contact:
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Contact</h2>
  <table>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th>Telephone / WeChat</th><td>{site.phone}</td></tr>
      <tr><th>WhatsApp</th><td>{site.phone}</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Commercial enquiries</th><td><a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a></td></tr>
      <tr><th>Sales and export</th><td><a href="mailto:laura@flourmillingpro.com">laura@flourmillingpro.com</a></td></tr>
      <tr><th>Administration / after-sales</th><td><a href="mailto:admin@flourmillingpro.com">admin@flourmillingpro.com</a></td></tr>
      <tr><th>Business hours</th><td>{site.hours}</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>4. Registration and qualification documents</h2>
  <p>
    The company's business licence, Unified Social Credit Code, import/export registration and
    certificate scopes are available to qualified buyers, freight forwarders, inspection agencies
    and regulators on request. We do not publish full registration numbers on the public website
    because they are used in commercial due-diligence and fraud checks; we will provide the relevant
    documents through a verified business channel.
  </p>
  <p>
    Certification references on this site include ISO 9001:2015, CE for selected models, an import
    and export licence, and National High-Tech Enterprise recognition. A certificate reference is
    not a statement that every product or project is covered; confirm the model-specific scope in
    the quotation or supplier-qualification pack.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Facilities and capability</h2>
  <p>
    The site covers approximately {site.area}, including about {site.workshop} of covered workshop.
    The company reports {site.employees} employees and more than {site.patents} patents. These
    figures are company-reported and should be verified against current records during a supplier
    audit.
  </p>
  <p>
    Product systems include wheat cleaning, roller milling, sifting, purification, packing, dust
    collection and complete plant engineering. Capacity ranges and model data are published for
    evaluation; the signed technical agreement defines the supplied scope.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Payment and contracting</h2>
  <p>
    Equipment is supplied against a written quotation and contract. Payments are normally made by
    bank transfer to the account named in the contract. We do not request payment-card details
    through this website, and we do not ask buyers to send funds to a different account without a
    verified contract amendment.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you receive a payment instruction that looks inconsistent with your contract, stop and
    verify it with the contact details on this page before paying.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Legal documents</h2>
  <p>
    See our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>,
    <a href="/cookie-policy/">Cookie Policy</a>,
    <a href="/terms/">Terms of Use</a>,
    <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a>,
    <a href="/export-compliance/">Export Compliance</a> and
    <a href="/compliance/">Compliance &amp; Ethics</a> pages.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
